### What steps can reproduce the bug?

I was looking for any changes to performance metrics after adopting `hono/proxy` for a Cloudflare Worker. Ideally a proxy would have minimal overhead, but there wasn't any real observable change. Nice work! 🎉

Is there any way to ensure the proxy helper doesn't add any unnecessary overhead?

This is a basic example of the original handler..

```js
app.post('/api/v1/example', (c) => {
  const honoRequest = c.req
  const request = c.req.raw
  const toforward = honoRequest.query('toforward')
  const exampleUrl = `https://example.com${toforward}`
  const headers = new Headers(request.headers)
  headers.delete('cookie')
  return fetch(exampleUrl, { body: request.body, headers, method: 'post' })
})
```

..and after adopting `hono/proxy`..

```js
app.post('/api/v1/example', (c) => {
  const toforward = c.req.query('toforward')
  const exampleUrl = new URL(toforward, 'https://example.com')
  return proxy(exampleUrl, {
    ...c.req,
    headers: {
      ...c.req.header(),
      Cookie: undefined,
    },
  })
})
```

