### Description

Prior to v2.14.0, you could use `Parameter()` with `description` and `schema_extra` to modify the generated schema for an Enum. This was changed in #3525. Apart from messing with `app.openapi_schema`, it seems like users have to modify the description via the Enum's docstring:

https://github.com/litestar-org/litestar/blob/ad8ad7205c8e07692b3b05b01ab052f091949b0b/litestar/_openapi/schema_generation/schema.py#L595

Note that v2.13.0 did not let you modify the schema's description through the Enum's docstring and I don't see feature being mentioned, so I think this was unintentional.

I'm not aware of a way to modify the Enum's generated schema in v2.16.0 that is as easy as modifying `schema_extra` like you could in v2.13.0.

