The optimised styles cache render commit 8ae3b5fcb3d1f4fce79392218129da475b65f752 introduced a subtle bug. It seems like the first line of the widget is reused in the padded sections of the widget, but when you use an outline that first line contains the top part of the 'border'. It looks like this:

<img width="921" height="583" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a6608cf-c44f-4716-8725-24f6d2ee6393" />

You can reproduce this with:

```py
from textual.app import App, ComposeResult
from textual.widgets import Static


class OutlineApp(App[None]):
    CSS = """
        Static {
            height: 15;
            padding-top: 5;
            padding-bottom: 5;
            outline: blue heavy;
        }
    """

    def compose(self) -> ComposeResult:
        for _ in range(10):
            yield Static("Lipsum")


OutlineApp().run()
```
It's probably an easy fix (or this optimisation may be reverted if the 'win' is only minimal) but I'm afraid to create another subtle bug if I try.
